From: Senemos Uke contributors
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: enforce the admitted Uke role and propagate PHY errors

The Uke eUSB2/repeater/WCD slice implements the OEM peripheral sequence.
The mainline legacy PHY interface does not set Qualcomm's host-mode flags,
so their existing flag check cannot reliably reject an unreviewed host DT.
Reject other Uke roles in glue probe before acquiring clocks or power.
Keep host/VBUS admission explicit while the ESP32 host graph is developed.

DWC3 normally ignores legacy usb_phy_init errors. For the Uke compatible,
propagate either error and shut down the successful USB2 initialization if
USB3 initialization fails. An unsuccessful PHY must not become a reported
working UDC. Preserve existing behavior for all other glue compatibles.

Source: Linux v7.2.9, drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c and dwc3-qcom.c
Source: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource
Commit: 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd
Files: drivers/usb/phy/phy-msm-snps-eusb2.c,
       drivers/usb/repeater/repeater-qti-pmic-eusb2.c
License: GPL-2.0-only

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -826,12 +826,19 @@
 
 static int dwc3_phy_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 {
+	bool uke = of_device_is_compatible(dwc->dev->of_node, "qcom,sm7675-dwc3");
 	int ret;
 	int i;
 	int j;
 
-	usb_phy_init(dwc->usb2_phy);
-	usb_phy_init(dwc->usb3_phy);
+	ret = usb_phy_init(dwc->usb2_phy);
+	if (ret && uke)
+		return ret;
+	ret = usb_phy_init(dwc->usb3_phy);
+	if (ret && uke) {
+		usb_phy_shutdown(dwc->usb2_phy);
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb2_ports; i++) {
 		ret = phy_init(dwc->usb2_generic_phy[i]);
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -670,6 +670,9 @@
 
 	qcom->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	qcom->uke = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,sm7675-dwc3");
+	if (qcom->uke && usb_get_dr_mode(dev) != USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EOPNOTSUPP,
+				     "Uke host PHY/repeater/VBUS profile is not admitted\n");
 
 	qcom->resets = devm_reset_control_array_get_optional_exclusive(dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(qcom->resets)) {
